    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0193" n="125" xml:id="pg125"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2042.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-08-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 16, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I transmit a copy of a letter which has
                    been handed to me by Colonel J. R. O’Bierne, late of the army of the United
                    States. This letter, dated the 10th of this month, and addressed to him by
                    William J. McCiure, is in regard to the case of his brother, who is one of the
                    Fenian prisoners, in relation to whom we have already had some correspondence.
                    Any proper measures which you can set in motion for the relief of McClure and
                    his associates will receive the hearty approval of the department.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
